{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1199304-what-are-praxes","id":1199304,"title":"What are Praxes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-24T22:23:03-07:00","id":1199304,"title":"What are Praxes","content":"Hi All - i think im missing something. My players have been creating characters via both rules and roleplay interaction using pbem. We have reached the point where they need to select a Praxes and im struggling. <br /> <br /> Do the players simply pick one of the rotes (regardless of rating) as their first Praxes ? e.g. one of my players has Time 3 and thinks he can take Rend Lifespan (which is Time 4) as a Praxes. Am i missing something ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6295-dargurd","name":"Dargurd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T22:42:40-07:00","id":1199308,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure you still need to be able to cast it yourself. After all, a Praxis in concept is your &quot;signature move.&quot; You can't have a signature move that you can't use.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Your player might be mistaking the flat cost of Praxes (one Experience for one Praxis, regardless of its Arcanum rating) for the ability to buy anything they want. The latte doesn't exist.<br /> <br /> Also, choose among rotes? Are you just referring to the published spells in the core book, or actual rotes? The latter has nothing to do with acquiring new Praxes, IIRC.<br /> <br /> EDIT: See p.112, on &quot;Praxes&quot; section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 03-25-2018, 01:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T22:46:51-07:00","id":1199309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1199304-what-are-praxes?p=1199308#post1199308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure you still need to be able to cast it yourself. After all, a Praxis in concept is your &quot;signature move.&quot; You can't have a signature move that you can't use.<br /> <br /> Also, choose among rotes? Are you just referring to the published spells in the core book, or actual rotes? The latter has nothing to do with acquiring new Praxes, IIRC.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And this is why im confused. <br /> <br /> The text in Character Creation reads as follows...<br /> <br /> <i>Your character has one Praxis per dot of Gnosis. Look to the Arcana descriptions again and choose spells to be your initial Praxes. Unlike Rotes, Praxes are not graded by dots; a spell of any rating is a single Praxis.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> So... im guessing im missing something. I keep jumping around the rule book to try and get a clearer picture but im still not sure what im missing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6295-dargurd","name":"Dargurd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T23:08:48-07:00","id":1199313,"title":"","content":"A character starting out with Time 3 can buy any Praxes that are based on Time 1, 2, or 3 spells. They all cost one Experience, even the ones based on Time 2 and Time 3 spells. But the character can't buy Time 4 and 5 spells as Praxes at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T23:13:38-07:00","id":1199315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1199304-what-are-praxes?p=1199313#post1199313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A character starting out with Time 3 can buy any Praxes that are based on Time 1, 2, or 3 spells. They all cost one Experience, even the ones based on Time 2 and Time 3 spells. But the character can't buy Time 4 and 5 spells as Praxes at the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok so do the players choose from the Rote list that is provided as part of each Arcana ? This is starting to make sense (i think lol).<br /> <br /> If im understanding correctly the Praxes is a more &quot;cast on the fly&quot; ability whereas the Rote equivalent you take your time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6295-dargurd","name":"Dargurd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T23:21:12-07:00","id":1199316,"title":"","content":"Rote list? Are you perhaps referring to the big list of spells in Chapter Five?<br /> <br /> There are three types of spells; improvised, rotes, and praxes. You're not mixing up the first two, are you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T23:26:03-07:00","id":1199318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1199304-what-are-praxes?p=1199316#post1199316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rote list? Are you perhaps referring to the big list of spells in Chapter Five?<br /> <br /> There are three types of spells; improvised, rotes, and praxes. You're not mixing up the first two, are you?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In character creation under Rotes in links to page 128 which is in Chapter 4. Under each Arcana it gives example rotes. In the next part of character creation it then tells you to select a Praxis. This is why im getting confused. You can start with up to 6 dots worth of Rotes but then talks about a free praxis regardless of rating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6295-dargurd","name":"Dargurd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T23:27:27-07:00","id":1199319,"title":"","content":"Rotes and praxes are different things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T23:30:41-07:00","id":1199320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1199304-what-are-praxes?p=1199319#post1199319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rotes and praxes are different things.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok so where do you select a praxes from or do you simply create one based on the rating examples under Arcana to help establish relative power or am i completely misreading this as thats how its starting to feel. - thanks for the help by the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6295-dargurd","name":"Dargurd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T23:35:09-07:00","id":1199321,"title":"","content":"The list in Chapter 5 are example spells of improvised spells, which inform players of what spells they can cast as improvised spells at that Arcanum rating, or take as rotes, or take as praxes. Different things sharing a common list to choose from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T23:38:29-07:00","id":1199324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1199304-what-are-praxes?p=1199321#post1199321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The list in Chapter 5 are example spells of improvised spells, which inform players of what spells they can cast as improvised spells at that Arcanum rating, or take as rotes, or take as praxes. Different things sharing a common list to choose from.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> OK so in that case apart from getting the rating part wrong i think both and I and my players are actually on the right path then. For the ease of use and as none of us have ever played this version of Mage before (all very used to Ascension) then we simply choose a Praxes from those lists a part of character creation .<br /> <br /> Thanks for the help very much appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6295-dargurd","name":"Dargurd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T01:14:39-07:00","id":1199327,"title":"","content":"You still have to be able to cast a praxis as an improvised spell.<br /> <br /> The rating refers tot he fact that you buy them for a flat XP fee, that doesn't change for praxes based on higher-dot spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T10:16:56-07:00","id":1199407,"title":"","content":"The base concept is that there are three ways to cast a spell; improvised, Rote and Praxes.<br /> \u200bImprovised is when you sit down in the moment and work out how to cast a spell for yourself. It is easy to make mistakes, especially when under pressure, and the one where you're most likely to realize afterwards that you forgot something or this would have worked better.<br /> <br /> \u200bRotes are when a Master of that Arcanum has sat down in the comfort of his sanctum and figured out how to cast the spell, then wrote it down. It is like a master chef figuring out how to create a great meal and then writing down a clear, step by step recipe that if followed properly will allow any smech to create the same great meal. You still have to be capable of casting the spell but it's like having the Master there to point out how to do it best.<br /> <br /> \u200bPraxes are over learning, you sit in your sanctum and practice casting a spell until you can do it without thinking, on reflex. It's like an athlete who practices so much that he burns the motions into muscle memory and no longer has to think about what he's doing. This method combines speed in the moment and gives a high likelihood of doing it right, even under pressure. The other advantage is that you don't need to be a Master to create one, you just have to practice.<br /> <br /> \u200bIn all three you have to be able to cast the spell in the first place, they are just different methods of doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T22:14:38-07:00","id":1199593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1199304-what-are-praxes?p=1199407#post1199407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The base concept is that there are three ways to cast a spell; improvised, Rote and Praxes.<br /> \u200bImprovised is when you sit down in the moment and work out how to cast a spell for yourself. It is easy to make mistakes, especially when under pressure, and the one where you're most likely to realize afterwards that you forgot something or this would have worked better.<br /> <br /> \u200bRotes are when a Master of that Arcanum has sat down in the comfort of his sanctum and figured out how to cast the spell, then wrote it down. It is like a master chef figuring out how to create a great meal and then writing down a clear, step by step recipe that if followed properly will allow any smech to create the same great meal. You still have to be capable of casting the spell but it's like having the Master there to point out how to do it best.<br /> <br /> \u200bPraxes are over learning, you sit in your sanctum and practice casting a spell until you can do it without thinking, on reflex. It's like an athlete who practices so much that he burns the motions into muscle memory and no longer has to think about what he's doing. This method combines speed in the moment and gives a high likelihood of doing it right, even under pressure. The other advantage is that you don't need to be a Master to create one, you just have to practice.<br /> <br /> \u200bIn all three you have to be able to cast the spell in the first place, they are just different methods of doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thankyou - that makes sense. Much appreciated. Getting my head around Awakening is proving hard but its going to be worth it in the long run ! Ive run White Wolf/Onyx Path games since they first came out in the early 90's but never ran Awakening. It could be a rough ride for a little while lol !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6295-dargurd","name":"Dargurd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T06:29:27-07:00","id":1199695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1199304-what-are-praxes?p=1199407#post1199407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The base concept is that there are three ways to cast a spell; improvised, Rote and Praxes.<br /> \u200bImprovised is when you sit down in the moment and work out how to cast a spell for yourself. It is easy to make mistakes, especially when under pressure, and the one where you're most likely to realize afterwards that you forgot something or this would have worked better.<br /> <br /> \u200bRotes are when a Master of that Arcanum has sat down in the comfort of his sanctum and figured out how to cast the spell, then wrote it down. It is like a master chef figuring out how to create a great meal and then writing down a clear, step by step recipe that if followed properly will allow any smech to create the same great meal. You still have to be capable of casting the spell but it's like having the Master there to point out how to do it best.<br /> <br /> \u200bPraxes are over learning, you sit in your sanctum and practice casting a spell until you can do it without thinking, on reflex. It's like an athlete who practices so much that he burns the motions into muscle memory and no longer has to think about what he's doing. This method combines speed in the moment and gives a high likelihood of doing it right, even under pressure. The other advantage is that you don't need to be a Master to create one, you just have to practice.<br /> <br /> \u200bIn all three you have to be able to cast the spell in the first place, they are just different methods of doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave's mentioned a further narrative distinction that bears emphasis: even outside the confines of spell factors, casting an improvised spell involves the mage accounting for a bunch of details and variables that are different in different circumstances \u2014 this is why it's significant that, as has been known, a rote is not just &quot;how to cast the spell&quot; but &quot;a particular mnemonic for how to cast the spell.&quot;<br /> <br /> Improvised casting is performing multiplication by treating the operation as a very long addition problem; a rote is knowing that multiples of five only end in 0 or 5, multiples of 2 are always even, etc. In this metaphor, then, a praxis is having done so much multiplication that you've memorized the times table; you don't have an optimized way to get to a pretty hard outcome, but you <i>do</i> have enough practice at doing the thing that you can pretty consistently do <i>very well</i> on goals within your means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T09:07:48-07:00","id":1199729,"title":"","content":"Praxes also commonly act as &quot;training wheels&quot; for future Legacy Attainments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T01:21:03-07:00","id":1201184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowbody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1199304-what-are-praxes?p=1199729#post1199729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__